TEXT -40 560 Left 2 ;Simulation Tip -> When simulating, prove V(ac+) - V(ac-) because the input sine wave has been divided\nSubtracting them gives you y=sin(x) \n \nThis is because diviing them gives us the following\nV(ac+) = sin(x)\nV(ac-) = sin(x+90) = cos(x)
